    "committer": "EllisPatrick <ellis.patrick@sydney.edu.au>",
    "message": "1.99.26: no adjusted design at a radius with no variation (adjusted_for \"none (no_variation)\")\n\nWhere a pair's response has no variation at a radius (no `to` cell has a `from` neighbour, or every one has), the\nunadjusted test is exactly 0 / 0 and the radius is left out. The adjusted design (adjustAbundance, covariates)\nturned those zeros into rounding noise (~1e-16), so the radius was kept with t = noise / noise and an arbitrary\ninfluence vector, which moved the davies, maxT and cauchy combinations arbitrarily. Now, when the unadjusted test\nhas no variation (!(se > 0)), no design is fitted: adjusted_for \"none (no_variation)\", p NaN, and nothing of the\nradius enters the combination (core pair_tests() and R's .cell_rows_test(); Kontextual uses the latter). The core's\ndesign_tests() also reports \"no_variation\" when the weighted residual sum of squares is at most (64 eps n)^2 times\nthe weighted sum of squares of the response (more than two conditions, survival, Hartung-Knapp); survival is\nadjusted for abundance only where the unadjusted test was done. With several radii, a radius where no pair's design\nwas fitted gets the other radii's effect columns (combining them stopped with an error before).\n\nChecks: refs.R (26 cases), maxt_refs.R (11) and memref.R (8) are identical() to 1.99.25's. t04 -> t05 of the\n10-type synthetic data (r = 5..125, age, abundance, davies) gives 0.772 (0.967; 0.772 with r = 115, 120 dropped),\nand with age perturbed by 1e-10 its p no longer moves. The davies_dev perturbation experiments (25 configurations,\nJackson, Keren, Schurch and synthetic): no combined p moves by more than 4e-9 (21-28% moved by > 0.01 before on\nthe adjusted real-data runs). New tests: empty and saturated radii give \"none (no_variation)\" for davies, maxT,\ncauchy and one radius; the combination equals that without the radius; a perturbed covariate; design_tests() on an\nexactly fitted response; three conditions and survival. Tests pass; R CMD check: the src/concaveman.hpp WARNIN",
    "time": 1792144094
  },
